# Built by build.ps1 from the sources beside it; never committed.
*.pk3
# EXCEPT the HUD panels pk3, kept here and committed at the owner's call (2026-09-14).
# Built by E:\DOOMWork\RS_VRPanels\build.ps1 -- quads, a sprite and script only, no
# Doom Eternal assets. RS_VRBody.pk3 stays ignored: it carries the Slayer arms.
# MOVED OUT 2026-09-18. The panels package no longer lands here at all -- its
# build.ps1 writes RS_VRPanels/RS_VRPanels.pk3 and the .zip the load order names,
# and the stale copy that used to sit here is in _old/stale_panels_copy_2026-09-18.
# The exception below is kept, dead, only so nobody re-adds the copy to satisfy it.
# !RS_VRPanels.pk3
__pycache__/
*.bak

# THE SLAYER ARMS' MESHES AND TEXTURES ARE DOOM ETERNAL ASSETS. They stay on disk and
# in the locally built pk3, and are NEVER committed or pushed -- this repo has a
# GitHub remote. Scoped to these two patterns only; PROVENANCE.md beside them is
# tracked and says where they came from.
models/slayer/*.iqm
models/slayer/*.png

# Mockup renders: some show the Slayer arms (Doom Eternal assets). Disk only.
renders/

# THE HELMET is the Doom Eternal Classic Slayer's (the owner's download, 2026-09-15). Same rule as the
# Slayer arms: meshes and textures stay on disk and in the local pk3, never pushed. PROVENANCE.md is tracked.
models/helmet/*.obj
models/helmet/*.png

# THE MARINE BODY (torso, shoulder pads, arms) and its fitted RS hands are made from the same Doom Eternal
# Classic Slayer download, and the retoned hand skin is matched to it. Same rule: disk and local pk3 only.
models/marine/*.iqm
models/marine/*.png

# THE PRAETOR / DARK AGES SLAYER is bigwig's GMod port of the Dark Ages Slayer (the owner's
# download, 2026-09-18). Exactly the same rule as the marine and the helmet above, and it was
# MISSING -- 150 MB of ripped meshes and textures sat untracked and would have gone up with the
# next `git add -A` onto a PUBLIC remote. Disk and local pk3 only; PROVENANCE.md is tracked.
models/praetor/*.iqm
models/praetor/*.png

# RENDERS OF THE BODIES ARE THE BODIES. `renders/` was already ignored for exactly this
# reason -- "some show the Slayer arms (Doom Eternal assets)" -- and an untextured render
# is still their geometry and their silhouette on a public remote. docs/ is not a loophole.
docs/*.png

# THE RIG RENDER IS THE EXCEPTION, AT THE OWNER'S REPEATED INSTRUCTION (2026-09-19, three
# times: "UPLOAD RENDERS TO README"). It is the one image this repo is meant to have. It is
# flat grey with the chains drawn on -- the joints, the proportions the seats are measured
# against, our own work -- which is exactly what render_rig.py was written to produce and
# why it exists. Narrow on purpose: this ONE file, not docs/ and not renders/.
!docs/rigs.png
